# Backend Rules — Laravel 11

## Architecture Flow
Request → Controller → FormRequest (validate) → Service → Repository → Model.
Never put Eloquent queries in Controllers or Services. Repositories own all DB queries.

## Response Format
Always use `ApiResponse` helper. Never return raw arrays or `response()->json()` directly.
```php
// ✅
return ApiResponse::success($data);
return ApiResponse::error('Insufficient stock', 422);

// ❌
return response()->json(['data' => $data]);
```

## Auth — JWT
Use `tymon/jwt-auth`. Return JWT in `httpOnly` cookie + JSON body on login.
Never store JWT in `localStorage` on the client.

## Order State Machine
Use `spatie/laravel-model-states`. Define allowed transitions explicitly.
```php
// ✅ Explicit transitions only
Pending::class => [Processing::class],
Processing::class => [Shipped::class, Cancelled::class],
```
Never allow arbitrary state changes via direct assignment.

## Stock Locking — Required Pattern
```php
// ✅ Always wrap in transaction + lockForUpdate
DB::transaction(function () use ($productId, $qty) {
    $product = Product::lockForUpdate()->findOrFail($productId);
    if ($product->stock < $qty) throw new InsufficientStockException();
    $product->decrement('stock', $qty);
});

// ❌ No lock = race condition = overselling
$product->decrement('stock', $qty);
```

## Webhook Handler (Pesapal)
- Route: `POST /api/webhooks/pesapal` — outside auth middleware
- Verify signature before any processing
- Log raw payload to `webhook_logs` table immediately
- Dispatch `ProcessPesapalWebhook` job — never process inline
- Check idempotency: skip if order already paid

## Search — Laravel Native (Postgres)
Use `pg_trgm` extension with raw queries. No third-party search service.
```php
$products = Product::whereRaw(
    "name % ? OR description % ?", [$term, $term]
)->orderByRaw("similarity(name, ?) DESC", [$term])->get();
```

## Feature Flags — Tax
Backend is single source of truth for all feature flags including tax.
```php
// Tax flag controls both rate application and amount storage
// Store separately: subtotal, tax_amount, total — never recompute post-order
```

## Rate Limiting (per route group)
```php
Route::middleware('throttle:5,1')->group(fn() => /* auth routes */);
Route::middleware('throttle:120,1')->group(fn() => /* public product routes */);
Route::middleware('throttle:10,1')->group(fn() => /* order creation */);
```

## Email — Resend
Use `resend/resend-laravel`. Local dev: Mailpit (docker-compose). Never hardcode SMTP creds.

## Testing — Pest
- Separate test DB: `DB_DATABASE=vill_shop_test` in `phpunit.xml`
- Use `RefreshDatabase` trait
- Feature tests for all API endpoints
- Unit tests for Services and critical Repository methods

## Logging
Use Monolog structured logging. Always include `request_id` (from `RequestId` middleware) in log context.
